The dashed curve is $y=f(x)$ and the solid curve is its reflection; the point $(1,2)$ maps to $(1,-2)$.
Which equation is the solid curve?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.3,0)--(4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.4)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-0.5:4.2,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*\x*\x-3*\x*\x+4.5*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-0.5:4.2,smooth,samples=61,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-(0.5*\x*\x*\x-3*\x*\x+4.5*\x)});
\node[gray,right] at (3.3,2.9) {$y=f(x)$};
\fill[gray] (1,2) circle (1.5pt) node[above] {$(1,2)$};
\fill (1,-2) circle (2pt) node[below] {$(1,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dashed curve is $y=f(x)$ and the solid curve is its reflection.
Across which axis has it been reflected?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.3,0)--(2.3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.3)--(0,3.3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-1.75:1.75,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.75:1.75,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-\x*\x});
\node[gray,right] at (1.4,2.9) {$y=f(x)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
